From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] unidrv, unidrvui, wineps, prntvpt: the custom size in every paper list; drivers' own settings in print tickets

What DYMO Connect (and WPF's print dialog) ask of a label printer's
Windows driver:

- unidrvui: the custom size (CUSTOMSIZE) was in DC_PAPERS and
  DC_PAPERNAMES but not DC_PAPERSIZE, so the lists did not line up. It is
  in every list at its place, named "Custom Size", its size the devmode's.
  A paper of the maker's own without an id got DMPAPER_USER (256) itself,
  the custom size's id; they start after it now.
- unidrvui, wineps (pscript5, ps5ui): the driver's own settings (a GPD's or
  PPD's features without a print schema keyword: DYMO's print density and
  quality, a laser's toner saving) for the print schema, through a
  Wine-internal export of the configuration DLL.
- prntvpt: they are in the print capabilities ("ns0000:DF_<feature>" with
  their options and names); a ticket's choice of one reaches the driver's
  devmode, and a devmode's comes back in its ticket. A devmode made from a
  ticket is the driver's whole devmode now, with its private part (it was
  the public fields only).

Test: test/drvui-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_CUSTOMSIZE, USERID,
DRVFEATURES, PTDRIVERFEATURES, PTFULLDEVMODE); test/printdrv-gate.sh still
covers ids against the GPD's own.
